## Context and authority

Filed from replicator 0003 (branch t0003-full-chain, commit ec32d2c) at
the author's request on 2026-11-26. Integration-review finding for
tracker 1552; complements 1569 (identification review). Request for
receiving Imagine, not an implementation authorization.

## Evidence

An inventory of the robustness work in 19 I4R discussion papers (fixed
sample: 9 from replicator's 0002 development cohort, 10 drawn with seed
20261126): `~/CNRS/projets/actifs/replicator/replications/chain-pilot-0003/i4r-robustness-inventory.md`
and `.json`, sample list beside them. 15 are replication reports, 4 are
meta-science or protocol. Extraction by Sonnet-class agents; three
entries spot-checked against the source text (papers 89, 100, 137), all
held; counts are approximate. No report in the sample concerns an RDD.

Observations (counts over the 15 reports or 127 checks; see the file):
- most frequent check categories: re-coding in other software, functional
  form/estimator, alternative controls, inference/clustering, sample
  restrictions, coding-error fixes (9 checks in 7 papers);
- identification critique in 5 of 15 reports, mostly inside the
  robustness section, own section in 1;
- original estimate beside each check in about half the checks; 4
  reports never do it; original column first is the common layout.

A first draft of a Carter (2024) plan in replicator showed the overfitting
risk: an RDD menu written from one paper would have entered the skill.

## Proposed split (for Imagine to accept, amend or reject)

Into SKILL.md § probe (design-independent):
1. Inventory the paper's own robustness (appendix and code) and propose
   only checks it does not already run; list the excluded ones.
2. Every code anomaly logged by `reproduce` becomes a candidate check.
3. The plan fixes its reporting rule beforehand: every check reported, no
   overall verdict from a count of passes.
4. Drop-one at the assignment or cluster unit, not the observation.
5. Validation hygiene: in a validation run, the executor and the signers
   have not read the paper's I4R report.
6. Sign-off modes: a person's line (default); a person's approval given
   in conversation, transcribed verbatim and labelled as transcription;
   an author-authorized model panel (replicator 0003 pilots Astra +
   Fable, rule in its PROTOCOL.md), recorded as a deviation until the
   pilot result is in.

Into a new reference (`references/robustness-menus.md`), menus per
design, each item citing either at least two I4R reports in an inventory
or a named methods source:
- from the sample: meta-analysis (publication-bias adjustments,
  REML vs DerSimonian-Laird, drop-one study); DiD (alternative treatment
  thresholds, event study, multiple-testing correction over interactions);
  experiments (pre-analysis-plan deviations, controls, outliers);
  observational panels (proxy validity, dropping dominant units,
  nonlinear controls);
- from methods literature, marked as such: RDD (bandwidth grid, kernel,
  polynomial order, donut, placebo cutoffs).

Stays in the paper folder, never in the skill: any variable, unit,
threshold or check specific to one paper.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Receiving Imagine records facts, duplicates (1568, 1569), ownership,
  standing rulings (rule 4: a person signs).
- [ ] If accepted: SKILL.md § probe gains the steps kept; the menus file
  exists with a source per item; no paper-specific item in either.
- [ ] The sign-off modes question is ruled after replicator 0003 reports.
